{"task": "Write a retrospective record of the Council's 21 December 2022 decision on Myanmar. Identify the draft, decision, representative positions, humanitarian access and ASEAN provisions, and the reporting instruction. Keep the Council president's procedural role separate from India's national statement. At most 130 words including any decision line.", "evidence": [{"id": "vote", "source": "https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/3998419?ln=en", "text": "The Council adopted draft S/2022/980 as resolution 2669 (2022), by 12 votes in favour, none against and three abstentions. The United Kingdom voted in favour. China, India and Russia abstained."}, {"id": "chair", "source": "https://documents.un.org/api/symbol/access?l=en&s=S%2FPV.9231&t=pdf", "text": "India held the Council presidency. The President called the vote and announced adoption. India's representative later explained the national abstention, then resumed the duties of President."}, {"id": "uk", "source": "https://documents.un.org/api/symbol/access?l=en&s=S%2FPV.9231&t=pdf", "text": "The United Kingdom submitted the draft and welcomed the result after consultations with Council members, ASEAN members and regional partners. It emphasized ending violence, humanitarian access and support for ASEAN efforts."}, {"id": "mandate", "source": "https://digitallibrary.un.org/record/3998406/files/S_RES_2669_%282022%29-EN.pdf", "text": "Resolution 2669 demands an immediate end to violence, calls for humanitarian access, and acknowledges ASEAN's central role. It requests the Secretary-General or his Special Envoy, in coordination with the ASEAN Special Envoy, to report orally to the Security Council by 15 March 2023 on UN support for the Five-Point Consensus."}, {"id": "india", "source": "https://documents.un.org/api/symbol/access?l=en&s=S%2FPV.9231&t=pdf", "text": "India praised the United Kingdom's consultation and noted neighbouring countries' concerns. It advocated quiet, constructive diplomacy and explained its abstention in light of those concerns."}], "answer": "The Council adopted draft S/2022/980 as resolution 2669 (2022) by 12 votes in favour, none against, and three abstentions. The United Kingdom voted in favour. China, India, and Russia abstained.

India's representative explained the national abstention citing neighbouring concerns, then resumed the duties of President. The proposal included humanitarian access and ASEAN provisions. A reporting instruction was issued mandating ASEAN reporting by 15 March 2023. The resolution demands ending violence.

The President called the vote and announced adoption. India held the Council presidency.", "choices": {"A": "clear", "B": "uncertain", "C": "failed"}}

